2026-05-09 16:04:05,543 - INFO - - This isn't really a free speech issue (legally—government isn't involved)—it's about *social* consequences
2026-05-09 16:04:05,543 - INFO - - The real questions are about *proportionality* and *context*, not whether accountability should exist at all
2026-05-09 16:04:05,543 - INFO - - Different cases look very different (a CEO's documented harassment vs. a misinterpreted tweet from 2009)
2026-05-09 16:04:05,543 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 16:04:05,543 - INFO - Rather than one being "right," you might find more productive ground asking: *Which specific cases are proportionate? How do we distinguish genuine accountability from pile-ons? What's a fair path to redemption?*
2026-05-09 16:04:05,543 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 16:04:05,543 - INFO - Those questions acknowledge both the value of accountability and the real costs of disproportionate punishment.
