2026-05-09 16:05:05,142 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 16:05:05,142 - INFO - **Why strict "never lie" fails:**
2026-05-09 16:05:05,143 - INFO - Classic counterexamples are hard to dismiss—hiding refugees from someone hunting them, or telling a patient a painful truth will resolve in days when it actually will take weeks (minor timing lie to reduce unnecessary suffering).
2026-05-09 16:05:05,143 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 16:05:05,143 - INFO - **Why "sometimes necessary" is more defensible:**
2026-05-09 16:05:05,143 - INFO - It acknowledges that honesty and other values (safety, compassion, autonomy) sometimes genuinely conflict, and that rigid rules can produce worse outcomes.
2026-05-09 16:05:05,143 - INFO - 
