2026-05-09 16:05:05,143 - INFO - - Most people *do* think some lies are justified, even if they don't admit it
2026-05-09 16:05:05,143 - INFO - - But this doesn't mean "lying is fine whenever"—it usually requires: serious stakes, no better alternative, and restraint
2026-05-09 16:05:05,143 - INFO - - Your instinct that lying is *generally* wrong is sound; it just has genuine exceptions
2026-05-09 16:05:05,144 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 16:05:05,144 - INFO - The productive disagreement isn't really "never vs. sometimes" but rather: **when do those exceptions actually apply?** That's harder and more interesting than either absolute position.
