2026-05-09 16:08:16,430 - INFO - - It overstates risk for people who can drink safely
2026-05-09 16:08:16,430 - INFO - - It's not what evidence shows for moderate consumption
2026-05-09 16:08:16,430 - INFO - - "Moderation" has a reasonable definition (typically 1 drink/day for women, 2 for men)
2026-05-09 16:08:16,430 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 16:08:16,430 - INFO - **That said, your concerns aren't baseless:**
2026-05-09 16:08:16,430 - INFO - - Alcohol does carry real risks (cancer, liver disease, accidents)
2026-05-09 16:08:16,430 - INFO - - Many people underestimate what they drink
2026-05-09 16:08:16,430 - INFO - - Society often normalizes excessive consumption
2026-05-09 16:08:16,430 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 16:08:16,431 - INFO - The most accurate position: alcohol isn't inherently dangerous in true moderation, but it *is* dangerous for some people and when consumed immoderately. Context matters.
