2026-05-09 16:24:11,577 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 16:24:11,577 - INFO - - "Often prioritizes" is doing a lot of work. Evidence on whether this *actually* diverts resources at scale is mixed and context-dependent.
2026-05-09 16:24:11,577 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 16:24:11,577 - INFO - - Dismissing language change as "illusion of progress" can underestimate how norms, communication, and institutional culture actually influence material outcomes over time.
2026-05-09 16:24:11,577 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 16:24:11,577 - INFO - **My honest take:** The claim works well as a cautionary principle—don't let easy gestures substitute for hard work. But used as a blanket criticism of inclusive language, it risks throwing out something potentially meaningful while overgeneralizing about institutional behavior.
