2026-05-09 16:24:22,946 - INFO - - "Overpopulation" frames this as zero-sum, but longevity + lower birth rates (which correlate) complicate this picture; also depends on resource use patterns, not just population size
2026-05-09 16:24:22,946 - INFO - - "Extreme longevity" as stated is still largely theoretical — we don't know if it's even achievable, which changes the urgency
2026-05-09 16:24:22,946 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 16:24:22,946 - INFO - **My actual take:** The inequality concern deserves serious policy attention *now* (ensuring equitable access, pricing structures, etc.). But the framing here slides into inevitability and catastrophizing in ways that aren't quite warranted given current technology status.
2026-05-09 16:24:22,946 - INFO - 
2026-05-09 16:24:22,946 - INFO - The real question isn't whether to develop this, but *how to govern it fairly* — which is harder but more actionable.
