2026-05-09 16:25:39,750 - INFO - - The framing assumes "claims of fragility" are mostly performative rather than reflecting actual struggles (mental health crises, precarity, bullying, discrimination). They may coexist with material comfort.
2026-05-09 16:25:39,750 - INFO - - "Elevation of victimhood as primary source of moral authority" is vague—who exactly is doing this, and how systematically? The claim feels rhetorically potent but harder to document precisely.
2026-05-09 16:25:39,750 - INFO - - The paradox (comfort + fragility claims) could have many explanations: social media amplifying niche voices, new visibility to previously silent struggles, legitimately new stressors, or just selection bias in what we notice online.
